"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", always all of the vertices has the same type. So we can calculate two numbers for each height "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". The sum of normal numbers of vertices with height "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the sum of their reverse numbers. Then instead of switching vertices in a height one by one each time, one can just switch the number for that height. The sum of numbers of heights after each query will be the answer for that query. since there are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" height each query can be performed in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") so the total running time will be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nq"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"  +  "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"  * 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/414/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"414D - Mashmokh and Water Tanks"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's suppose instead of a tank there is a pile at each vertex and instead of water the game is played on tiles. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's denote distance of each vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the root by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"depth"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("}